  "verbalization": "Cyanocobalamin, through multiple binding interactions, is linked to the Cobalamin Biosynthetic Process and the Cobalamin (cbl, Vitamin B12) Transport And Metabolism pathways, all of which are participated by Mmab. This suggests that Mmab plays a role in the biosynthesis or transport of cobalamin, potentially through interactions with Cyanocobalamin. The evidence indicates that Cyanocobalamin may act as a regulatory or structural component in the metabolic pathway involving Mmab, with Mmab being a central actor in the process of cobalamin metabolism. The overlapping participation of Mmab in multiple pathways related to cobalamin suggests a functional link between Cyanocobalamin and Mmab, possibly through a shared regulatory mechanism or a direct interaction in the metabolic network. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Mmab in cobalamin-related processes, with Cyanocobalamin serving as a key molecule in this network.",
